WEBVTT

00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:30.515
Even though I studied comparative
physiology and evolutionary biology

00:03:30.515 --> 00:03:32.598
as an undergrad --

00:03:32.598 --> 00:03:37.136
I had even written my senior 
thesis on Darwinian theory --

00:03:37.136 --> 00:03:39.856
learning about the 
significant overlap

00:03:39.856 --> 00:03:42.592
between the disorders of 
animals and humans,

00:03:42.592 --> 00:03:48.311
it came as a much needed 
wake-up call for me.

00:03:48.311 --> 00:03:52.799
So I started wondering,
with all of these overlaps,

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:58.317
how was it that I had never
thought to ask a veterinarian,

00:03:58.317 --> 00:04:00.844
or consult the veterinary literature,